            "sources": {
                "pole": "Poled standing on her floor: her beam bears a man standing far more stiffly than the narrowest canoe polers stand in (bin/lib/hulls/physics.py). No source shows a currach poled, so he stands where a canoe poler does, about a foot aft of her middle (ACA, Canoe Poling), off his thwart. His hands end the shove at his hip (0.530 of a 1.756 m stature: Drillis & Contini 1966; ANSUR II, Gordon et al. 2014); his eyes at vanilla's standing 1.7 m",
                "sideDrag": "Hide over round ribs: the round-bilged hull's cross-flow drag",
                "oars": "Her two oars on their tholes (the oar's own sources); from blade to blade across her by the model (bin/lib/hulls/currach.py), over her drive's sweep, with each blade's area under the water as his hands hold the grips at his lower ribs: the tholes at her gunwale 0.38 m abaft her thwart (Dingle's, Hornell 1938; none is given for Aran), each 3 m oar's loom reaching from its pin to her middle (Hornell's rule for the inboard) and the rest of it outboard to its blade"
            }
