            "sources": {
                "parts": "By the model (bin/lib/hulls/currach.py): her hide 5 mm thick at hide's density over her ribs, stringers and gunwales of laths 1 by 6 cm of ash and a thwart pole 9 cm across; and her two 3 m oars",
                "seconds": "Held for the real time over sixty, as her build's work is: a patch of hide sewn over a hole as long as sewing one section of her cover, some twenty minutes; rubbing rendered fat into her hide some ten minutes (estimates)",
                "shell": "Raw cowhide is 2 to 6 mm thick. A blow springs back off the hide unless a lath backs it where it lands: by the model, the share of her sides and her bottom her ribs, stringers and keelson lie against (bin/lib/hulls/wounds.py). A breaker presses the hide onto the laths, each 1 cm deep bending over the span between her longitudinal laths. A knock, a ram or rapids presses the hide onto the lath behind where it lands: wet hide stretches to 60% before it parts (pickled cowhide, 26.6 MPa at 60% elongation; Tensile Properties of Indigenous Kenyan Boran Pickled and Tanned Bovine Hide), so on a lath it passes the blow on, and the lath, 1 by 6 cm of ash, breaks by its impact bending work across its section; between two laths, the longitudinals and the ribs crossing them as far apart as her model draws them, it sags as a membrane until its pull breaks both. Hornell (British Coracles and Irish Curraghs, 1938) has curragh builders cover the frame's rough ends, which would otherwise cut the hide: a broken lath's end is what opens it",
                "seep": "A seam where one hide meets the next weeps once the tallow has washed out of it, and Aran crews dressed their currachs every few days: a seam across her weeps some 15 L an hour for each 2.3 m of it (bin/lib/hulls/physics.py), as long as her model draws her girth where her sections meet. A currach from before her build is covered in prepared hide over her eight sections, with the two seams the three large hides of her old recipe had",
                "cover": "The hides a vessel is covered with as her build lays them; one from before her build is covered with prepared hides, as the grid made her"
            },
